# TypeScript output emitted next to its input.
#
# A project with no `outDir` writes each `.js`/`.d.ts` beside the `.ts` it came
# from. `examples/tsconfig.json` was one, and its `include` takes every
# package's sources as inputs of its own, so a single `tsc -b` of one example
# left 1461 generated files through `packages/*/src`. That one is fixed at the
# source (`noEmit`); this is what keeps the next stray `tsc` invocation out of
# a commit. Nothing hand-written lives under a `src/` directory with these
# extensions - `packages/api-ui/assets/*.js` is outside `src`, and the
# `logerror.js` files sit at their package roots.

**/src/**/*.js
**/src/**/*.js.map
**/src/**/*.d.ts
**/src/**/*.d.ts.map
examples/_lib/*/index.js
examples/_lib/*/index.js.map
examples/_lib/*/index.d.ts
